


## 3. Entity Framework
Entity Framework is an Object Relational Mapper (ORM) that maps objects between the systam and a database. Entity frameworks takes database tables and turn them into objects. An object normally represents a one row in a database. 

#### To install Entity Framework Run 
```dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFramework.SqlServer```

```dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools```

```dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design```



#### Migrations
Install .NET CLI first by running the command:
```dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef```

Check the installation 
```dotnet ef```

Run code to intialize a migration to database
```dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate```

Create a database, table and schem by running the command
```dotnet ef database update```

A new folder called `Migrations` will be created out of this that contains the migration configurations.